{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-21T01:57:53.860Z","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a2d731112b51f7b87</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>call_f6a423975e074028979e3818</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/tmp/claude-1000/-home-warner-openvela/6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323/tasks/a2d731112b51f7b87.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Analyze mboot FSBL config\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Here is the comprehensive analysis of the mboot/FSBL configuration for external flash boot on the ATK-DNN647 board.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Board and MCU Identification\n\n- **Board name**: ATK-DNN647\n- **MCU**: STM32N647X0 (Cortex-M55, ARMv8.1-M)\n- **Board config directory**: `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/`\n- **HSE crystal**: 48 MHz\n- **CPU frequency**: 800 MHz (PLL: HSE/6*100/1)\n\n---\n\n## 2. External Flash Chip Configuration\n\n**Flash chip**: Macronix **MX25UM25645G** (256 Mbit = 32 MB)\n\nKey defines in `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/mpconfigboard.h`:\n```c\n#define MICROPY_HW_XSPIFLASH_SIZE_BITS_LOG2     (28)   // 2^28 = 256 Mbit\n#define MBOOT_SPIFLASH_ADDR                     (0x70000000)\n#define MBOOT_SPIFLASH_BYTE_SIZE                (32 * 1024 * 1024)\n#define MBOOT_SPIFLASH_LAYOUT                   \"/0x70000000/8192*4Kg\"\n```\n\nThe XSPI peripheral is configured with **Macronix memory type** in `DCR1`:\n```c\n1 &lt;&lt; XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_Pos // Macronix mode\n```\n\n---\n\n## 3. Hardware Interface: XSPI2 (not QSPI, not FMC)\n\nThe external flash uses the **XSPI2** peripheral (the STM32N6's enhanced octo-SPI interface). This is distinct from the older QSPI peripheral. The driver is at:\n\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c`\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.h`\n\n**Pin mapping** (from `pins.csv`, lines 173-184):\n| Signal | Pin | Port |\n|--------|-----|------|\n| CS | PN1 | XSPI2 |\n| SCK | PN6 | XSPI2 |\n| DQS | PN0 | XSPI2 |\n| IO0 | PN2 | XSPI2 |\n| IO1 | PN3 | XSPI2 |\n| IO2 | PN4 | XSPI2 |\n| IO3 | PN5 | XSPI2 |\n| IO4 | PN8 | XSPI2 |\n| IO5 | PN9 | XSPI2 |\n| IO6 | PN10 | XSPI2 |\n| IO7 | PN11 | XSPI2 |\n\nAll pins use **alternate function 9** on port PN (1.8V IO bank), configured at `VERY_HIGH` speed.\n\n---\n\n## 4. XSPI Operating Modes\n\nThe XSPI driver supports two modes and defaults to **octal DTR (DOPI)** mode:\n\n**SPI mode (1-line, STR)** -- `xspi_memory_map_111()`:\n- Command `0x13` (READ4B), 1-line instruction/address/data, no dummy cycles\n- Used as fallback/initialization mode\n\n**Octal DTR (8-line, DOPI)** -- `xspi_memory_map_888()` (default):\n- Command `0xEE11` (8DTRD), 8-line instruction/address/data, all DTR\n- 20 dummy cycles for read\n- DQS enabled for data strobe\n- 16-bit instruction size\n\n**Mode switching** (in `xspi_init()`, line 187-192):\n```c\nif (1) {\n    xspi_switch_to_dtr();    // WREN + write REG[0x00]=0x02 via WRSCUR (0x72)\n    xspi_memory_map_888();   // Enable memory-mapped DOPI mode\n} else {\n    xspi_memory_map_111();   // SPI fallback\n}\n```\n\nThe DTR switch uses Macronix-specific commands:\n- `0x06` (WREN) in SPI mode\n- `0x72` (WRSCUR) to write register at address 0x00000000 with value 0x02 (DOPI mode)\n- `0x06F9` (WREN in DTR), `0x728D` (WRSCUR in DTR) to switch back to SPI\n\n---\n\n## 5. XIP (Execute-in-Place) Memory Map\n\nThe XSPI2 memory-mapped region is at **0x70000000** (defined in `xspi_flash2.xip_base`). This means the CPU can directly fetch instructions and read data from external flash as if it were regular memory.\n\nThe XSPI clock source is HCLK with a prescaler of 4:\n```c\n#define MICROPY_HW_XSPI_PRESCALER (4) // F_CLK = F_AHB/4\n```\n\n---\n\n## 6. Complete Boot Flow\n\n### Stage 0: Hardware Boot ROM\n\nThe STM32N647's built-in boot ROM runs first. It loads the first **512 KB** of external flash (starting at offset 0) into **SRAM2** at address **0x34180000**. The first 1024 bytes (0x400) are a header, so the actual code starts at **0x34180400**.\n\nThis is documented in the linker script `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/mboot/stm32_memory_n6.ld`:\n```\n/* On N6, the hardware bootloader loads the first 512k of external flash into\n   the upper part of SRAM2 AXI S, starting at 0x34180000.  The first 1024 bytes\n   is a header. Then comes the actual code, starting with the vector table. */\nFLASH_BL (rx) : ORIGIN = 0x34180400, LENGTH = 31744   /* ~31K for mboot code */\nRAM (xrw)     : ORIGIN = 0x341e0000, LENGTH = 128K\n```\n\n### Stage 1: FSBL / mboot (First Stage Boot Loader)\n\nThe mboot Makefile (`/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/mboot/Makefile`) uses the FSBL system file when building mboot:\n```makefile\nifeq ($(BUILDING_MBOOT),1)\nSYSTEM_FILE = .../system_stm32$(MCU_SERIES)xx_fsbl.o\n```\n\nThe FSBL startup sequence:\n1. **`startup_stm32n647xx_fsbl.s`** (`/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/stm32lib/CMSIS/STM32N6xx/Source/Templates/gcc/startup_stm32n647xx_fsbl.s`): Sets stack pointer, calls `SystemInit()`, copies `.data`, zeros `.bss`, calls `main()`\n\n2. **`system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c`** (`/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/lib/stm32lib/CMSIS/STM32N6xx/Source/Templates/system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c`): Sets VTOR, clears SAU regions, resets XSPI2/XSPIM peripherals, configures VDDADC, VREFBUF\n\n3. **`mboot/main.c`** `stm32_main()` entry (line 1514):\n   - Calls `stm32_system_init()`\n   - Sets `SCB-&gt;VTOR = 0x34180400` (mboot's own vector table)\n   - Reads `TAMP_S-&gt;BKP31R` for reset mode (N6-specific)\n   - Calls `MBOOT_BOARD_EARLY_INIT()` which invokes `mboot_board_early_init()`\n\n4. **`mboot_board_early_init()`** in `board.c` (line 84):\n   - Configures VDDIO2/3/4 voltage domains (VDDIO3 at 1.8V for XSPI pins)\n   - Programs BSEC OTP fuse for high-speed IO optimization on VDDIO3\n   - Configures SMPS supply + voltage scaling (Scale 0)\n   - **Calls `xspi_init()`** -- this is the critical step that initializes XSPI2 and switches the flash to DOPI memory-mapped mode\n   - Pre-configures PLL2/PLL4 and IC17/IC18 for DCMIPP + CSI camera clocks\n\n5. **Back in `stm32_main()`**:\n   - Checks boot pin and reset mode to decide whether to enter DFU or boot application\n   - Initializes the SPI flash: `mp_spiflash_init(MBOOT_SPIFLASH_SPIFLASH)`\n   - Enters USB DFU loop for firmware update, or tries to boot the application\n\n6. **Application boot**: `try_enter_application()` reads the stack pointer from `APPLICATION_ADDR` (0x70080000) and jumps to it via `branch_to_application()`\n\n### Stage 2: Main Application (runs from XSPI flash via XIP)\n\nThe main firmware is linked to run from external flash at **0x70080000**:\n```makefile\nTEXT0_ADDR = 0x70080000\nLD_FILES = boards/stm32n657x0.ld boards/common_n6_flash.ld\n```\n\nFrom `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/stm32n657x0.ld`:\n```\nEXT_FLASH (rx) : ORIGIN = 0x70080000, LENGTH = 1536K\n```\n\nThe `common_n6_flash.ld` linker script places critical code (ISR vectors, spiflash driver, XSPI driver, board standby code) in IRAM for performance and because flash write operations require exiting memory-mapped mode.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Flash Layout Map\n\n| Address Range | Size | Purpose |\n|---|---|---|\n| 0x70000000 - 0x7007FFFF | 512 KB | Stage 1 (mboot/FSBL), loaded to SRAM by HW boot ROM |\n| 0x70080000 - 0x7017FFFF | 1.5 MB | Main MicroPython firmware (XIP) |\n| 0x70180000 - 0x7057FFFF | 4 MB | MicroPython filesystem (FAT/LittleFS) |\n| 0x70580000 - 0x71FFFFFF | ~27.5 MB | Remaining flash (unused/reserved) |\n\nThe filesystem partition starts at offset 4 MB from the flash base:\n```c\n#define MICROPY_HW_BDEV_SPIFLASH_OFFSET_BYTES   (4 * 1024 * 1024)\n#define MICROPY_HW_BDEV_SPIFLASH_SIZE_BYTES     (4 * 1024 * 1024)\n```\n\n---\n\n## 8. DFU Programming Interface\n\nThe mboot exposes USB DFU over USB1 OTG HS (in FS mode) at `USB1_OTG_HS_IRQHandler`. The flash layout string reported to DFU tools is:\n```\n/0x70000000/8192*4Kg\n```\nThis means 8192 sectors of 4 KB each starting at address 0x70000000 (32 MB total).\n\nThe `deploy-trusted` target in the mboot Makefile uses STM32 SigningTool to create a signed FSBL image:\n```makefile\n$(STM32_CUBE_PROGRAMMER)/bin/STM32_SigningTool_CLI -bin $^ -nk -of 0x80000000 -t fsbl -o $@ -hv $(STM32_N6_HEADER_VERSION) --align\n```\n\nAn external loader file `MX25UM25645G_ATK-CNN647B_ExtMemLoader.stldr` is needed for STM32CubeProgrammer.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Key File Paths Summary\n\n**Board configuration**:\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/mpconfigboard.h` -- all hardware defines, mboot config, pin assignments\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/mpconfigboard.mk` -- build system config, linker file selection, USE_MBOOT=1\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/bdev.c` -- SPI flash block device config (XSPI2 + xspi_proto)\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/board.c` -- mboot_board_early_init(), VDDIO config, PLL2/PLL4 setup, xspi_init() call\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/pins.csv` -- XSPIM_P2 pin definitions (PN0-PN11)\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/boards/ATK_DNN647/stm32n6xx_hal_conf.h` -- HSE=48MHz, LSE=32kHz, MCE stubs for N647\n\n**Mboot (bootloader)**:\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/mboot/main.c` -- main bootloader logic, DFU, SPI flash init, application jump\n- `/home/warner/openvela/atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/mboot/mboot.h` -