RAM (loaded by the debugger in DEV mode, or by an FSBL\n   * from external XSPI flash in normal boot).\n   *\n   * AXI SRAM layout (from CMSIS stm32n657xx.h):\n   *   AXISRAM1:     0x34000000  1 MB\n   *   AXISRAM2:     0x34100000  1 MB\n   *   AXISRAM3:     0x34200000  448 KB\n   *   AXISRAM4:     0x34270000  448 KB\n   *   AXISRAM5:     0x342E0000  448 KB\n   *   AXISRAM6:     0x34350000  448 KB\n   *   CACHEAXIRAM:  0x343C0000  256 KB\n   *   Total:        4 MB (end = 0x34400000)\n   */\n  #define STM32_SRAM_SIZE  (4 * 1024 * 1024)\n  #define STM32_NPORTS     (12)   /* GPIO ports A-H + N, O, P, Q */\n  #define STM32_NUSART     (1)    /* USART1 */\n  ```\n- `irq.h` -- Includes `stm32n6xx_irq.h`\n- `stm32n6xx_irq.h` -- IRQ definitions for STM32N657xx (195 external interrupts). Comment: \"These interrupt vectors are based on the STM32N657xx CMSIS device header (stm32n657xx.h IRQn_Type enumeration).\"\n\n---\n\n## 3. NuttX Board Support: `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/`\n\n**Directory:** `/home/warner/openvela/nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/`\n\n**Files:**\n- `Kconfig` -- Empty stub (just `if ARCH_BOARD_NUCLEO_N657X0_Q` / `endif`)\n- `CMakeLists.txt`\n- `include/board.h` -- Board header, comment: \"All STM32N6 architectures must provide the following entry point\"\n- `scripts/flash.ld` -- Linker script with key comment:\n  ```\n  /* The STM32N657X0 has no internal flash.  In DEV boot mode, code is loaded\n   * directly into SRAM by the ST-Link debugger at 0x34000400.  The first\n   * 1 KiB of SRAM is reserved for the boot ROM header.\n   */\n  MEMORY { sram (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x34000400, LENGTH = 4193280 }\n  ```\n- `scripts/Make.defs`\n- `src/` -- Board source files:\n  - `nucleo-n657x0-q.h`, `stm32_boot.c`, `stm32_bringup.c`\n  - `stm32_autoleds.c`, `stm32_userleds.c`\n  - `Make.defs`, `CMakeLists.txt`\n- `configs/` -- Three defconfig profiles:\n  - **`leds/defconfig`**: `CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP=\"stm32n6\"`, `CONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N657X0=y`, `CONFIG_AR