{"parentUuid":"4fd2c43b-b77a-45c9-a27d-fcfbe1670ef9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_7c33dc575dd943acb2cc91eb","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_a511deaeb70044da99463c36","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/warner/openvela/nucleo-n657x0-q-fsbl-guide.md","content":"# NUCLEO-N657X0-Q FSBL + 外部Flash配置完整指南\n\n## 背景知识\n\n### STM32N6 的特殊之处\n- **STM32N657X0 没有内部Flash** — 代码必须从外部 XSPI Flash 运行（XIP）或由调试器加载到 SRAM\n- **启动流程**：硬件 Boot ROM → FSBL（第一阶段引导加载程序）→ 主应用程序\n- **硬件 Boot ROM** 会将外部 Flash 前 512KB 加载到 SRAM2（0x34180000），跳过 1024 字节头后从 0x34180400 开始执行 FSBL\n- **FSBL 的核心任务**：初始化 XSPI 外设，将 Flash 切换到高速模式（Octal DTR），启用内存映射，然后跳转到主应用\n\n### 参考项目分析\n- **ATK-DNN647 板**：STM32N647X0 + MX25UM25645G (256Mbit/32MB) — 已有完整 FSBL/mboot\n- **NUCLEO-N657X0 MicroPython**：STM32N657X0 + MX25UM51245G (512Mbit/64MB) — 已有完整 FSBL/mboot\n- **NuttX nucleo-n657x0-q**：仅有 SRAM 运行模式，无 XSPI 支持\n\n### Nucleo-N657X0-Q 硬件信息\n| 项目 | 值 |\n|------|-----|\n| MCU | STM32N657X0 (Cortex-M55) |\n| 外部 Flash | MX25UM51245G (512Mbit = 64MB) |\n| XSPI 接口 | XSPI2 |\n| XSPI 基地址 | 0x5802A000（控制器）/ 0x70000000（内存映射） |\n| Flash 引脚 | PN0-PN11（VDDIO3 域，1.8V） |\n| HSE | 48 MHz |\n\n### Flash 布局（参考 MicroPython Nucleo 配置）\n| 地址范围 | 大小 | 用途 |\n|----------|------|------|\n| 0x70000000 - 0x7007FFFF | 512KB | FSBL（被硬件 Boot ROM 加载到 SRAM） |\n| 0x70080000 - 0x7087FFFF | 8MB | 主固件（XIP 从 Flash 执行） |\n| 0x70880000 - 0x73FFFFFF | ~55MB | 文件系统 / 数据存储 |\n\n---\n\n## 第一步：创建 XSPI 驱动\n\n### 1.1 创建头文件 `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.h`\n\n```c\n/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.h\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * XSPI (Extended SPI) driver for STM32N6 external flash.\n * Supports Macronix MX25UM51245G in SPI and Octal DTR modes.\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#ifndef __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_STM32N6_XSPI_H\n#define __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_STM32N6_XSPI_H\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include <nuttx/spi/qspi.h>\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Function Prototypes\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#ifdef __cplusplus\nextern \"C\"\n{\n#endif\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_initialize\n *\n * Description:\n *   Initialize the XSPI2 peripheral and configure the external flash\n *   for memory-mapped (XIP) access in Octal DTR mode.\n *\n * Returned Value:\n *   OK on success; a negated errno on failure.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nint stm32n6_xspi_initialize(void);\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_get_qspi_dev\n *\n * Description:\n *   Get the QSPI device interface for the XSPI2 flash.\n *   This allows the standard MTD/spiflash drivers to access the flash\n *   for read/write/erase operations.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nstruct qspi_dev_s *stm32n6_xspi_get_qspi_dev(void);\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable\n *\n * Description:\n *   Enable memory-mapped mode on XSPI2.\n *   The flash is accessible at 0x70000000 for XIP.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable(void);\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit\n *\n * Description:\n *   Exit memory-mapped mode to allow direct flash commands.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit(void);\n\n#ifdef __cplusplus\n}\n#endif\n\n#endif /* __ARCH_ARM_SRC_STM32N6_STM32N6_XSPI_H */\n```\n\n### 1.2 创建源文件 `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c`\n\n这个文件是核心，参考 `atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c` 移植：\n\n```c\n/****************************************************************************\n * arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c\n *\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * XSPI2 driver for STM32N6 — controls external Macronix MX25UM51245G\n * flash in SPI and Octal DTR (DOPI) modes with memory-mapped XIP.\n *\n * Reference: atk-dnn647-micropython/ports/stm32/xspi.c\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include <nuttx/arch.h>\n#include <nuttx/clock.h>\n#include <nuttx/kmalloc.h>\n#include <nuttx/spi/qspi.h>\n\n#include <assert.h>\n#include <errno.h>\n#include <debug.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"stm32n6_gpio.h\"\n#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_memorymap.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_rcc.h\"\n#include \"hardware/stm32n6xxx_xspi.h\"  /* 需要创建或从 HAL 导入 */\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* XSPI2 is used for external flash */\n\n#define XSPI2_AF              9         /* Alternate function for PN pins */\n#define XSPI_FLASH_BASE       0x70000000\n#define XSPI_FLASH_SIZE       (64 * 1024 * 1024)  /* 512Mbit = 64MB */\n\n/* Clock prescaler: F_CLK = F_AHB / PRESCALER\n * With HCLK=50MHz, prescaler=4 gives 12.5MHz for init, can be lowered later\n */\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER\n#  define CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER  4\n#endif\n\n/* CS high time: nCS stays high for (CSHT+1) cycles */\n\n#ifndef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES\n#  define CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES  2\n#endif\n\n/* Flash size in log2(bytes) - 1: MX25UM51245G = 512Mbit = 64MB = 2^26 */\n\n#define XSPI_FLASH_SIZE_LOG2  26\n\n/* Macronix commands for SPI mode */\n\n#define CMD_READ4B            0x13    /* 4-byte address read */\n#define CMD_WRITE4B           0x12    /* 4-byte address program */\n#define CMD_SE4B              0x21    /* 4-byte sector erase (4KB) */\n#define CMD_WREN              0x06    /* Write enable */\n#define CMD_RDSR              0x05    /* Read status register */\n#define CMD_WRSCUR            0x72    /* Write security register */\n#define CMD_RSTEN             0x66    /* Reset enable */\n#define CMD_RESET             0x99    /* Reset */\n\n/* Macronix commands for Octal DTR mode (each byte is complemented) */\n\n#define CMD_8DTRD             0xee11  /* Octal DTR read */\n#define CMD_8DTRP             0x12ed  /* Octal DTR program (4B addr) */\n#define CMD_8DTRSE            0x21de  /* Octal DTR sector erase (4B) */\n#define CMD_8DTRWREN          0x06f9  /* Octal DTR write enable */\n#define CMD_8DTRRDSR          0x05fa  /* Octal DTR read status */\n#define CMD_8DTRWRSCUR        0x728d  /* Octal DTR write security reg */\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Data\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nstatic bool g_xspi_dtr_enabled = false;\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Configure a GPIO pin as XSPI alternate function at VERY_HIGH speed */\n\nstatic inline void xspi_pinconfig(uint32_t pinset)\n{\n  stm32n6_configgpio(pinset | GPIO_SPEED_VERY_HIGH);\n}\n\n/* Read 1 line (SPI mode) */\n\nstatic int xspi_read_111(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi,\n                          uint8_t cmd, bool has_addr,\n                          uint32_t addr, size_t len, uint8_t *dest)\n{\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? 1 : 0;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (1 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);  /* indirect read */\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos)  |  /* data on 1 line */\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos) |  /* 32-bit address */\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);     /* instruction on 1 line */\n  xspi->TCR = 0;                    /* 0 dummy cycles */\n  xspi->DLR = len - 1;\n  xspi->IR = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->AR = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while ((xspi->SR >> XSPI_SR_FLEVEL_Pos) == 0)\n        {\n          if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *dest++ = *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->DR;\n    }\n\n  xspi->FCR = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Write 1 line (SPI mode) */\n\nstatic int xspi_write_111(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi,\n                           uint8_t cmd, bool has_addr,\n                           uint32_t addr, size_t len,\n                           const uint8_t *src)\n{\n  uint32_t dmode = (len == 0) ? 0 : 1;\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? 1 : 0;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (0 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);  /* indirect write */\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (dmode << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos)  |\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos)     |\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->TCR = 0;\n\n  if (len != 0)\n    {\n      xspi->DLR = len - 1;\n    }\n\n  xspi->IR = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->AR = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while (!(xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_FTF))\n        {\n          if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->DR = *src++;\n    }\n\n  while (!(xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TCF))\n    {\n      if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n        {\n          return -EIO;\n        }\n    }\n\n  xspi->FCR = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  while (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_BUSY);\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Read Octal DTR mode */\n\nstatic int xspi_read_888_dtr(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi,\n                              uint16_t cmd, bool has_addr,\n                              uint32_t addr, uint32_t dummy,\n                              size_t len, uint8_t *dest)\n{\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? 4 : 0;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (1 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DQSE_Pos)  |  /* DQS enabled */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DDTR_Pos)  |  /* data DTR */\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |  /* 8 lines */\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ADDTR_Pos) |  /* address DTR */\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ISIZE_Pos) |  /* 16-bit instruction */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IDTR_Pos)  |  /* instruction DTR */\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);   /* 8 lines */\n  xspi->TCR = dummy << XSPI_TCR_DCYC_Pos;\n  xspi->DLR = len - 1;\n  xspi->IR = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->AR = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while ((xspi->SR >> XSPI_SR_FLEVEL_Pos) == 0)\n        {\n          if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *dest++ = *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->DR;\n    }\n\n  xspi->FCR = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Write Octal DTR mode */\n\nstatic int xspi_write_888_dtr(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi,\n                               uint16_t cmd, bool has_addr,\n                               uint32_t addr, size_t len,\n                               const uint8_t *src)\n{\n  uint32_t dmode = (len == 0) ? 0 : 4;\n  uint32_t admode = has_addr ? 4 : 0;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (0 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DDTR_Pos)  |\n    (dmode << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ADDTR_Pos) |\n    (admode << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ISIZE_Pos) |\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IDTR_Pos)  |\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->TCR = 0;\n\n  if (len != 0)\n    {\n      xspi->DLR = len - 1;\n    }\n\n  xspi->IR = cmd;\n\n  if (has_addr)\n    {\n      xspi->AR = addr;\n    }\n\n  while (len--)\n    {\n      while (!(xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_FTF))\n        {\n          if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n            {\n              return -EIO;\n            }\n        }\n\n      *(volatile uint8_t *)&xspi->DR = *src++;\n    }\n\n  while (!(xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TCF))\n    {\n      if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TEF)\n        {\n          return -EIO;\n        }\n    }\n\n  xspi->FCR = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n  while (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_BUSY);\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/* Switch flash from SPI mode to Octal DTR (DOPI) mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_switch_to_dtr(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi)\n{\n  uint8_t buf[4];\n\n  /* WREN in SPI mode */\n\n  xspi_write_111(xspi, CMD_WREN, false, 0, 0, NULL);\n\n  /* Wait WEL=1 */\n\n  for (unsigned int i = 0; i < 100; i++)\n    {\n      xspi_read_111(xspi, CMD_RDSR, false, 0, 1, buf);\n      if (buf[0] & 0x02)\n        {\n          break;\n        }\n    }\n\n  /* Write security register to enable DOPI mode:\n   * Address 0x00000000, data = 0x02\n   */\n\n  buf[0] = 0x02;\n  xspi_write_111(xspi, CMD_WRSCUR, true, 0x00000000, 1, buf);\n\n  g_xspi_dtr_enabled = true;\n}\n\n/* Enable memory-mapped mode in SPI (1-line) mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_memory_map_111(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi)\n{\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);\n  xspi->TCR = 0;\n  xspi->IR  = CMD_READ4B;\n  xspi->LPTR = 1024;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (3 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);  /* memory-mapped */\n}\n\n/* Enable memory-mapped mode in Octal DTR mode */\n\nstatic void xspi_memory_map_888(XSPI_TypeDef *xspi)\n{\n  xspi->CCR =\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DQSE_Pos)  |   /* DQS enabled */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_DDTR_Pos)  |   /* data DTR */\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_DMODE_Pos) |   /* 8 lines */\n    (3 << XSPI_CCR_ADSIZE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ADDTR_Pos) |   /* address DTR */\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_ADMODE_Pos)|\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_ISIZE_Pos) |   /* 16-bit instruction */\n    (1 << XSPI_CCR_IDTR_Pos)  |   /* instruction DTR */\n    (4 << XSPI_CCR_IMODE_Pos);    /* 8 lines */\n\n  xspi->TCR = 20 << XSPI_TCR_DCYC_Pos;  /* 20 dummy cycles */\n  xspi->IR  = CMD_8DTRD;\n  xspi->LPTR = 1024;\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (3 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);  /* memory-mapped */\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_initialize\n *\n * Description:\n *   Initialize XSPI2, configure pins, reset flash, switch to Octal DTR,\n *   and enable memory-mapped mode for XIP.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nint stm32n6_xspi_initialize(void)\n{\n  XSPI_TypeDef *xspi = XSPI2;\n\n  spiinfo(\"XSPI2: Initializing external flash...\\n\");\n\n  /* ---- Step 1: Configure XSPI2 GPIO pins (PN0-PN11, AF9) ---- */\n\n  /* NOTE: You need to define these pin macros in your board.h or\n   * a dedicated pin header. The pins are:\n   *   PN0  = DQS\n   *   PN1  = CS (NCS)\n   *   PN2  = IO0\n   *   PN3  = IO1\n   *   PN4  = IO2\n   *   PN5  = IO3\n   *   PN6  = SCK\n   *   PN8  = IO4\n   *   PN9  = IO5\n   *   PN10 = IO6\n   *   PN11 = IO7\n   *\n   * All use AF9, VDDIO3 domain (1.8V), VERY_HIGH speed.\n   */\n\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_DQS);   /* PN0 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_CS);    /* PN1 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO0);   /* PN2 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO1);   /* PN3 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO2);   /* PN4 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO3);   /* PN5 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_SCK);   /* PN6 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO4);   /* PN8 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO5);   /* PN9 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO6);   /* PN10 */\n  xspi_pinconfig(GPIO_XSPI2_IO7);   /* PN11 */\n\n  /* ---- Step 2: Enable clocks and release reset ---- */\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR, 0, RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST |\n                                        RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST |\n                                        RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST);\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5RSTR, RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI1RST |\n                                     RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPI2RST |\n                                     RCC_AHB5RSTR_XSPIMRST, 0);\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB5ENR, 0, RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPIMEN |\n                                      RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI1EN  |\n                                      RCC_AHB5ENR_XSPI2EN);\n\n  /* Set XSPI2 kernel clock source = HCLK */\n\n  /* NOTE: The exact register bit depends on the RCC_CCIPRx layout.\n   * Refer to RM0486 for your specific clock routing.\n   */\n\n  /* ---- Step 3: Configure XSPIM in direct mode ---- */\n\n  XSPI1->CR &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPI2->CR &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPIM->CR = 0;   /* direct mode */\n\n  /* ---- Step 4: Configure XSPI2 peripheral ---- */\n\n  xspi->CR =\n    (3 << XSPI_CR_FTHRES_Pos) |  /* 4 bytes FIFO threshold */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_MSEL_Pos)   |  /* FLASH 0 */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_CSSEL_Pos)  |  /* use NCS1 */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_DMM_Pos)    |  /* no dual-memory */\n    (1 << XSPI_CR_TCEN_Pos)   |  /* timeout enabled */\n    (0 << XSPI_CR_EN_Pos);       /* disabled for now */\n\n  xspi->DCR1 =\n    (1 << XSPI_DCR1_MTYP_Pos)               |  /* Macronix memory type */\n    ((XSPI_FLASH_SIZE_LOG2 - 3 - 1) << XSPI_DCR1_DEVSIZE_Pos) |\n    ((CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_CS_HIGH_CYCLES - 1) << XSPI_DCR1_CSHT_Pos) |\n    (0 << XSPI_DCR1_FRCK_Pos)   |  /* CLK not free-running */\n    (0 << XSPI_DCR1_CKMODE_Pos);   /* CLK idles low */\n\n  xspi->DCR2 =\n    ((CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER - 1) << XSPI_DCR2_PRESCALER_Pos);\n  xspi->DCR3 = 0;\n  xspi->DCR4 = 0;  /* refresh disabled (NOR flash) */\n  xspi->TCR = 0;\n\n  /* Enable XSPI2 */\n\n  xspi->CR |= XSPI_CR_EN;\n\n  /* Re-configure XSPIM */\n\n  XSPI1->CR &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPI2->CR &= ~XSPI_CR_EN;\n  XSPIM->CR = 0;\n  xspi->CR |= XSPI_CR_EN;\n\n  /* ---- Step 5: Switch flash to Octal DTR (DOPI) mode ---- */\n\n  xspi_switch_to_dtr(xspi);\n\n  /* ---- Step 6: Enable memory-mapped mode for XIP ---- */\n\n  xspi_memory_map_888(xspi);\n\n  spiinfo(\"XSPI2: Flash accessible at 0x%08x (64MB, Octal DTR XIP)\\n\",\n          XSPI_FLASH_BASE);\n\n  return OK;\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_exit(void)\n{\n  XSPI_TypeDef *xspi = XSPI2;\n\n  if (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_BUSY)\n    {\n      xspi->CR |= XSPI_CR_ABORT;\n      while (!(xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_TCF));\n      xspi->FCR = XSPI_FCR_CTCF;\n      while (xspi->SR & XSPI_SR_BUSY);\n    }\n\n  xspi->CR = (xspi->CR & ~XSPI_CR_FMODE_Msk) |\n             (0 << XSPI_CR_FMODE_Pos);  /* indirect write */\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32n6_xspi_memory_mapped_enable(void)\n{\n  if (g_xspi_dtr_enabled)\n    {\n      xspi_memory_map_888(XSPI2);\n    }\n  else\n    {\n      xspi_memory_map_111(XSPI2);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第二步：创建 FSBL（第一阶段引导加载程序）\n\nFSBL 是在 NuttX 主固件之前运行的小程序，负责初始化硬件和 XSPI Flash。\n\n### 2.1 FSBL 链接脚本 `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/fsbl.ld`\n\n```ld\n/* FSBL runs from SRAM2 after being loaded by the hardware boot ROM.\n *\n * The hardware ROM loads the first 512KB of external flash into SRAM2\n * starting at 0x34180000.  The first 1024 bytes (0x400) is a header,\n * so the actual FSBL code starts at 0x34180400.\n *\n * Available SRAM2 for FSBL: ~31KB (0x34180400 to 0x3419FFFF)\n * Stack: in SRAM at 0x341E0000 (128KB)\n */\n\nMEMORY\n{\n    fsbl_code (rx)  : ORIGIN = 0x34180400, LENGTH = 31744   /* ~31KB */\n    fsbl_ram  (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x341E0000, LENGTH = 128K\n}\n\nOUTPUT_ARCH(arm)\nENTRY(fsbl_entry)\n\nSECTIONS\n{\n    .text : {\n        _sfsbl_text = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.vectors)\n        *(.text .text.*)\n        *(.fixup)\n        *(.gnu.warning)\n        *(.rodata .rodata.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.t.*)\n        _efsbl_text = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > fsbl_code\n\n    .data : {\n        _sfsbl_data = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.data .data.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.d.*)\n        . = ALIGN(4);\n        _efsbl_data = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > fsbl_ram AT > fsbl_code\n\n    _efsbl_data_load = LOADADDR(.data);\n\n    .bss : {\n        _sfsbl_bss = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.bss .bss.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.b.*)\n        *(COMMON)\n        . = ALIGN(4);\n        _efsbl_bss = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > fsbl_ram\n}\n```\n\n### 2.2 FSBL 主程序 `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_fsbl.c`\n\n```c\n/****************************************************************************\n * boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_fsbl.c\n *\n * FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader) for NUCLEO-N657X0-Q.\n *\n * This runs from SRAM2 after the hardware boot ROM loads it from\n * external flash offset 0.  Its job:\n *   1. Configure VDDIO3 (1.8V) for XSPI pins\n *   2. Initialize XSPI2 and switch flash to Octal DTR mode\n *   3. Enable memory-mapped mode (XIP)\n *   4. Jump to the main NuttX application at 0x70080000\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Included Files\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n#include <nuttx/config.h>\n#include <stdint.h>\n#include <string.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Pre-processor Definitions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Application entry point in external flash */\n\n#define APP_ENTRY_ADDR    0x70080000\n\n/* BSEC OTP fuse for VDDIO3 high-speed IO optimization */\n\n#define BSEC_HW_CONFIG_ID     124\n#define BSEC_HWS_HSLV_VDDIO3  (1 << 15)\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Configure VDDIO domains for XSPI flash pins */\n\nstatic void fsbl_config_vdd(void)\n{\n  /* Enable PWR, BSEC, SYSCFG clocks */\n\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_AHB4ENR, 0, RCC_AHB4ENR_PWREN);\n  modifyreg32(STM32_RCC_APB4ENR2, 0, RCC_APB4EN2_BSECEN |\n                                       RCC_APB4EN2_SYSCFGEN);\n\n  /* Program OTP fuse for VDDIO3 high-speed mode if not already set */\n\n  /* NOTE: The actual BSEC register access depends on your HAL/LL version.\n   * The MicroPython reference uses HAL_BSEC_OTP_Read/Program.\n   * For NuttX, you may need to use direct register access or add BSEC support.\n   */\n\n  /* Configure VDDIO3 for 1.8V (XSPI pins PN0-PN11 are on VDDIO3) */\n\n  /* NOTE: Use PWR register writes. Refer to RM0486 Section 5.\n   * LL_PWR_EnableVddIO3();\n   * LL_PWR_SetVddIO3VoltageRange(LL_PWR_VDDIO_VOLTAGE_RANGE_1V8);\n   * Enable IO compensation on SYSCFG->VDDIO3CCCR\n   */\n\n  /* Configure VDDIO2 and VDDIO4 for 3.3V */\n\n  /* Configure SMPS supply + voltage scaling for higher performance */\n\n  /* HAL_PWREx_ConfigSupply(PWR_SMPS_SUPPLY); */\n  /* HAL_PWREx_ControlVoltageScaling(PWR_REGULATOR_VOLTAGE_SCALE0); */\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: fsbl_entry\n *\n * Description:\n *   Entry point for the FSBL.  Called by the hardware boot ROM after\n *   loading this code from flash offset 0 into SRAM2 at 0x34180400.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid fsbl_entry(void)\n{\n  /* Set vector table to our location */\n\n  SCB->VTOR = 0x34180400;\n\n  /* Clear SAU (Security Attribution Unit) regions */\n\n  /* NOTE: SAU registers are at 0xE000EDD0.  The FSBL system file\n   * (system_stm32n6xx_fsbl.c) typically handles this.\n   */\n\n  /* Configure power domains for XSPI */\n\n  fsbl_config_vdd();\n\n  /* Initialize XSPI2 and enable memory-mapped flash */\n\n  stm32n6_xspi_initialize();\n\n  /* Jump to main application in external flash (XIP) */\n\n  /* The application's vector table is at 0x70080000:\n   *   [0] = Initial stack pointer\n   *   [1] = Reset handler address\n   */\n\n  uint32_t app_sp  = *(volatile uint32_t *)(APP_ENTRY_ADDR);\n  uint32_t app_pc  = *(volatile uint32_t *)(APP_ENTRY_ADDR + 4);\n\n  /* Set stack pointer */\n\n  __asm__ volatile (\"msr msp, %0\" :: \"r\" (app_sp));\n\n  /* Jump to application */\n\n  void (*app_reset)(void) = (void (*)(void))app_pc;\n  app_reset();\n\n  /* Should never reach here */\n\n  for (;;);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第三步：修改链接脚本支持 XIP\n\n### 3.1 创建 XIP 链接脚本 `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/xip.ld`\n\n```ld\n/* XIP (Execute-In-Place) from external XSPI flash.\n *\n * The FSBL has already initialized XSPI2 and enabled memory-mapped mode.\n * Code at 0x70080000 runs directly from flash.\n * Writable data (.data, .bss) goes to SRAM.\n */\n\n/* Memory map:\n *   0x70080000 - 0x7087FFFF  8MB   External flash (code, rodata) - XIP\n *   0x34000400 - 0x343FFFFF  ~4MB  SRAM (data, bss, heap)\n */\n\nMEMORY\n{\n    flash (rx)  : ORIGIN = 0x70080000, LENGTH = 8192K\n    sram  (rwx) : ORIGIN = 0x34000400, LENGTH = 4193280\n}\n\nOUTPUT_ARCH(arm)\nENTRY(_stext)\n\nSECTIONS\n{\n    .text : {\n        _stext = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.vectors)\n        *(.text .text.*)\n        *(.fixup)\n        *(.gnu.warning)\n        *(.rodata .rodata.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.t.*)\n        *(.glue_7)\n        *(.glue_7t)\n        *(.got)\n        *(.gcc_except_table)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.r.*)\n        _etext = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > flash\n\n    .init_section : {\n        _sinit = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        KEEP(*(SORT_BY_INIT_PRIORITY(.init_array.*) SORT_BY_INIT_PRIORITY(.ctors.*)))\n        KEEP(*(.init_array EXCLUDE_FILE(*crtbegin.o *crtbegin?.o *crtend.o *crtend?.o) .ctors))\n        _einit = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > flash\n\n    .ARM.extab : {\n        *(.ARM.extab*)\n    } > flash\n\n    __exidx_start = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    .ARM.exidx : {\n        *(.ARM.exidx*)\n    } > flash\n    __exidx_end = ABSOLUTE(.);\n\n    /* .data is stored in flash (load address) but runs from SRAM */\n\n    .data : {\n        _eronly = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        _sdata = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.data .data.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.d.*)\n        CONSTRUCTORS\n        . = ALIGN(4);\n        _edata = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > sram AT > flash\n\n    .bss : {\n        _sbss = ABSOLUTE(.);\n        *(.bss .bss.*)\n        *(.gnu.linkonce.b.*)\n        *(COMMON)\n        . = ALIGN(4);\n        _ebss = ABSOLUTE(.);\n    } > sram\n\n    /* Stabs debugging sections. */\n    .stab 0 : { *(.stab) }\n    .stabstr 0 : { *(.stabstr) }\n    .stab.excl 0 : { *(.stab.excl) }\n    .stab.exclstr 0 : { *(.stab.exclstr) }\n    .stab.index 0 : { *(.stab.index) }\n    .stab.indexstr 0 : { *(.stab.indexstr) }\n    .comment 0 : { *(.comment) }\n    .debug_abbrev 0 : { *(.debug_abbrev) }\n    .debug_info 0 : { *(.debug_info) }\n    .debug_line 0 : { *(.debug_line) }\n    .debug_pubnames 0 : { *(.debug_pubnames) }\n    .debug_aranges 0 : { *(.debug_aranges) }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第四步：修改板级配置\n\n### 4.1 更新 `board.h` — 添加 XSPI 引脚定义和时钟配置\n\n在 [board.h](nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/include/board.h) 中添加：\n\n```c\n/* XSPI2 GPIO pins for external flash (Port PN, AF9, VDDIO3 domain 1.8V) */\n\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_DQS  (GPIO_XSPI2_DQS_0)   /* PN0 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_CS   (GPIO_XSPI2_CS_0)     /* PN1 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO0  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO0_0)    /* PN2 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO1  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO1_0)    /* PN3 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO2  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO2_0)    /* PN4 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO3  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO3_0)    /* PN5 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_SCK  (GPIO_XSPI2_SCK_0)    /* PN6 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO4  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO4_0)    /* PN8 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO5  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO5_0)    /* PN9 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO6  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO6_0)    /* PN10 */\n#define GPIO_XSPI2_IO7  (GPIO_XSPI2_IO7_0)    /* PN11 */\n\n/* NOTE: The actual GPIO macro names depend on your pinmux header.\n * You need to create or find the pin definitions for STM32N6 PN pins\n * with AF9.  Check if nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/hardware/stm32n6xxx_pinmap.h\n * has these definitions.  If not, you need to add them.\n */\n```\n\n### 4.2 更新 `stm32_bringup.c` — 初始化 XSPI\n\n在 [stm32_bringup.c](nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_bringup.c) 中添加：\n\n```c\n#include \"stm32n6_xspi.h\"\n\nint stm32_bringup(void)\n{\n  int ret;\n\n  /* ... existing initialization ... */\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI\n  /* Initialize XSPI2 external flash.\n   * NOTE: If running via FSBL, XSPI is already initialized.\n   * This is only needed when running from SRAM (DEV mode via debugger).\n   */\n\n  ret = stm32n6_xspi_initialize();\n  if (ret < 0)\n    {\n      syslog(LOG_ERR, \"ERROR: Failed to initialize XSPI2: %d\\n\", ret);\n    }\n#endif\n\n  /* ... rest of bringup ... */\n\n  return OK;\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第五步：创建 Kconfig 配置\n\n### 5.1 添加 XSPI Kconfig `nuttx/arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Kconfig`\n\n在现有 Kconfig 文件中添加：\n\n```kconfig\nconfig STM32N6_XSPI\n    bool \"XSPI external flash support\"\n    default n\n    ---help---\n        Enable the XSPI (Extended SPI) driver for external flash\n        on STM32N6 boards.  This supports Macronix MX25UM series\n        NOR flash in SPI and Octal DTR modes with memory-mapped\n        XIP (Execute-In-Place) capability.\n\nif STM32N6_XSPI\n\nconfig STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER\n    int \"XSPI clock prescaler\"\n    default 4\n    ---help---\n        XSPI clock = HCLK / prescaler.\n        With HCLK=50MHz and prescaler=4, XSPI clock = 12.5MHz.\n        Lower values give faster flash access but may be unstable.\n\nconfig STM32N6_XSPI_FLASH_SIZE_MB\n    int \"External flash size (MB)\"\n    default 64\n    ---help---\n        Size of the external XSPI flash in megabytes.\n        MX25UM51245G = 64MB, MX25UM25645G = 32MB.\n\nconfig STM32N6_FSBL\n    bool \"Build as FSBL (First Stage Boot Loader)\"\n    default n\n    ---help---\n        Build this image as an FSBL that initializes XSPI flash\n        and jumps to the main application.  The FSBL runs from\n        SRAM2 after being loaded by the hardware boot ROM.\n\nendif # STM32N6_XSPI\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第六步：创建 defconfig\n\n### 6.1 创建 XIP defconfig `nuttx/boards/arm/stm32n6/nucleo-n657x0-q/configs/xip/defconfig`\n\n```ini\n# NUCLEO-N657X0-Q: XIP from external XSPI flash\n# Requires FSBL to be flashed at flash offset 0 first.\n\nCONFIG_ARCH=\"arm\"\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD=\"nucleo-n657x0-q\"\nCONFIG_ARCH_BOARD_NUCLEO_N657X0_Q=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_CHIP=\"stm32n6\"\nCONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N657X0=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_CHIP_STM32N6=y\nCONFIG_ARCH_INTERRUPTSTACK=4096\nCONFIG_ARCH_STACKDUMP=y\nCONFIG_BOARD_LOOPSPERMSEC=21000\nCONFIG_BUILTIN=y\nCONFIG_HAVE_CXX=y\nCONFIG_HAVE_CXXINITIALIZE=y\nCONFIG_IDLETHREAD_STACKSIZE=4096\nCONFIG_INIT_ENTRYPOINT=\"nsh_main\"\nCONFIG_NSH_BUILTIN_APPS=y\nCONFIG_NSH_FILEIOSIZE=512\nCONFIG_NSH_READLINE=y\nCONFIG_RAW_BINARY=y\nCONFIG_RR_INTERVAL=200\nCONFIG_SCHED_WAITPID=y\nCONFIG_STM32_USART1=y\nCONFIG_SYSTEM_NSH=y\nCONFIG_USART1_SERIAL_CONSOLE=y\n\n# XSPI external flash\nCONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI=y\nCONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_PRESCALER=4\nCONFIG_STM32N6_XSPI_FLASH_SIZE_MB=64\n\n# RAM configuration\nCONFIG_RAM_START=0x34000400\nCONFIG_RAM_SIZE=4193280\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第七步：构建和烧录流程\n\n### 7.1 整体流程\n\n```\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│  1. 编译 FSBL (fsbl.bin)                             │\n│     - 链接到 0x34180400 (SRAM2)                      │\n│     - 初始化 XSPI2, 切换 Flash 到 Octal DTR          │\n│     - 启用内存映射 (XIP)                              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  2. 签名 FSBL → fsbl-signed.bin                      │\n│     - 使用 STM32 SigningTool 添加启动头               │\n│     - 头部大小 = 1024 字节                            │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  3. 编译主固件 (nuttx.bin)                            │\n│     - 链接到 0x70080000 (外部 Flash XIP)              │\n├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤\n│  4. 烧录到外部 Flash                                  │\n│     - offset 0x000000: fsbl-signed.bin (512KB)       │\n│     - offset 0x080000: nuttx.bin (主固件)             │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n```\n\n### 7.2 详细步骤\n\n#### 步骤 A：编译 FSBL\n\n```bash\ncd /home/warner/openvela/nuttx\n\n# 配置 FSBL 构建\nmake distclean\n./tools/configure.sh nucleo-n657x0-q:fsbl\n\n# 编译\nmake -j$(nproc)\n\n# 输出: nuttx.bin (FSBL 二进制)\n```\n\n#### 步骤 B：签名 FSBL\n\nSTM32N6 的硬件 Boot ROM 要求 FSBL 前有签名头部：\n\n```bash\n# 使用 STM32 SigningTool (随 STM32CubeProgrammer 提供)\nSTM32_SigningTool_CLI \\\n  -bin nuttx.bin \\\n  -nk \\\n  -of 0x80000000 \\\n  -t fsbl \\\n  -o fsbl-signed.bin \\\n  -hv 2.3 \\\n  --align\n```\n\n参数说明：\n- `-bin nuttx.bin`：输入 FSBL 二进制\n- `-nk`：无加密密钥（开发模式）\n- `-of 0x80000000`：输出格式偏移\n- `-t fsbl`：标记为 FSBL 类型\n- `-hv 2.3`：头版本（参考 MicroPython 配置）\n- `--align`：对齐\n\n#### 步骤 C：编译主固件\n\n```bash\n# 重新配置为主固件\nmake distclean\n./tools/configure.sh nucleo-n657x0-q:xip\nmake -j$(nproc)\n\n# 输出: nuttx.bin (主固件)\n```\n\n#### 步骤 D：烧录到外部 Flash\n\n使用 STM32CubeProgrammer：\n\n```bash\n# 方法1: 使用 STM32CubeProgrammer CLI\nSTM32_Programmer_CLI \\\n  -c port=SWD \\\n  -w fsbl-signed.bin 0x70000000 \\\n  -w nuttx.bin 0x70080000 \\\n  -v \\\n  -rst\n\n# 方法2: 使用外部加载器 (.stldr)\n# 需要下载 MX25UM51245G_STM32N6570-NUCLEO.stldr\nSTM32_Programmer_CLI \\\n  -c port=SWD \\\n  --extload MX25UM51245G_STM32N6570-NUCLEO.stldr \\\n  -w fsbl-signed.bin 0x70000000 \\\n  -w nuttx.bin 0x70080000 \\\n  -v \\\n  -rst\n```\n\n### 7.3 开发模式（不使用 FSBL）\n\n在开发阶段，可以直接用调试器将固件加载到 SRAM 运行：\n\n```bash\n# 使用原来的 nsh defconfig（纯 SRAM 运行）\nmake distclean\n./tools/configure.sh nucleo-n657x0-q:nsh\nmake -j$(nproc)\n\n# 通过 ST-Link 加载到 SRAM\nSTM32_Programmer_CLI -c port=SWD -w nuttx.bin 0x34000400 -rst\n```\n\n---\n\n## 第八步：验证 Flash 读写功能\n\n### 8.1 在 NuttX shell 中测试\n\n```bash\nnsh> ls /dev\n# 应该看到 /dev/mtdblock0 (或其他 MTD 设备)\n\nnsh> dd if=/dev/mtdblock0 of=/tmp/flash_test bs=4096 count=1\nnsh> hexdump -C /tmp/flash_test | head\n\n# 写入测试\nnsh> echo \"Hello Flash\" > /tmp/test.txt\nnsh> dd if=/tmp/test.txt of=/dev/mtdblock0 bs=4096 count=1\n\n# 掉电后重新上电，读回验证\nnsh> dd if=/dev/mtdblock0 of=/tmp/readback bs=4096 count=1\nnsh> cat /tmp/readback\n# 应该看到 \"Hello Flash\"\n```\n\n### 8.2 使用 LittleFS 实现掉电保存\n\n```bash\n# 在 defconfig 中添加\nCONFIG_FS_LITTLEFS=y\nCONFIG_MTD=y\n\n# 在 shell 中挂载\nnsh> mklittlefs -f /dev/mtdblock1\nnsh> mount -t littlefs /dev/mtdblock1 /mnt\nnsh> echo \"Power-off safe data\" > /mnt/config.txt\nnsh> cat /mnt/config.txt\n# 掉电后重新上电\nnsh> mount -t littlefs /dev/mtdblock1 /mnt\nnsh> cat /mnt/config.txt\n# 数据仍然存在\n```\n\n---\n\n## 关键差异总结：ATK-DNN647 vs Nucleo-N657X0-Q\n\n| 项目 | ATK-DNN647 (参考) | Nucleo-N657X0-Q (目标) |\n|------|-------------------|----------------------|\n| MCU | STM32N647X0 | STM32N657X0 |\n| Flash 芯片 | MX25UM25645G (256Mbit) | MX25UM51245G (512Mbit) |\n| Flash 大小 | 32MB | 64MB |\n| SIZE_LOG2 | 28 | 29 |\n| XSPI 引脚 | PN0-PN11 (相同) | PN0-PN11 (相同) |\n| VDDIO 域 | VDDIO3 1.8V | VDDIO3 1.8V |\n| 外部加载器 | MX25UM25645G_ATK.stldr | MX25UM51245G_STM32N6570-NUCLEO.stldr |\n\n两个板子的 XSPI 引脚映射完全相同（都是 PN0-PN11, AF9），主要区别是 Flash 容量和型号。\n\n---\n\n## 文件清单\n\n需要创建/修改的文件：\n\n| 文件 | 操作 | 说明 |\n|------|------|------|\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.h` | 新建 | XSPI 驱动头文件 |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/stm32n6_xspi.c` | 新建 | XSPI 驱动实现 |\n| `arch/arm/src/stm32n6/Kconfig` | 修改 | 添加 XSPI 配置项 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/include/board.h` | 修改 | 添加 XSPI 引脚定义 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_bringup.c` | 修改 | 调用 XSPI 初始化 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/xip.ld` | 新建 | XIP 链接脚本 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/scripts/fsbl.ld` | 新建 | FSBL 链接脚本 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/src/stm32_fsbl.c` | 新建 | FSBL 主程序 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/configs/xip/defconfig` | 新建 | XIP 构建配置 |\n| `boards/.../nucleo-n657x0-q/configs/fsbl/defconfig` | 新建 | FSBL 构建配置 |\n\n---\n\n## 常见问题\n\n### Q1: 为什么需要 FSBL？\nSTM32N6 没有内部 Flash，硬件 Boot ROM 只能加载 512KB 到 SRAM。FSBL 负责初始化 XSPI 控制器，让 CPU 可以通过内存映射直接从外部 Flash 执行代码（XIP）。\n\n### Q2: 不用 FSBL 可以吗？\n可以，但只能在 DEV 模式下通过调试器将代码加载到 SRAM 运行。掉电后代码丢失。\n\n### Q3: XSPI 引脚的电压域问题\nXSPI 引脚（PN0-PN11）在 VDDIO3 域上，必须配置为 1.8V 模式。需要通过 BSEC OTP 熔丝启用高速 IO 优化。这个操作是**一次性不可逆**的（烧熔丝）。\n\n### Q4: 如何调试 FSBL？\n1. 先用 DEV 模式（调试器直接加载到 SRAM）调试基本功能\n2. 确认 XSPI 初始化成功后，再制作签名 FSBL 烧录到 Flash\n\n### Q5: 时钟配置差异\nMicroPython 使用 HSE 48MHz 达到 800MHz CPU 频率。NuttX 当前配置使用 HSI 64MHz 只到 200MHz。如果需要更高性能，需要：\n1. 确认板上有 48MHz HSE 晶振（Nucleo 板应该有）\n2. 修改 PLL 配置\n3. 可能需要配置 SMPS 和电压调节器\n"}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":2853,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":53760}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"143a9904-f90d-4cb2-a882-1b0e76ce5758","timestamp":"2026-08-21T02:03:31.145Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD"}
