{"parentUuid":"d810c0e9-95ee-4e4a-b850-195d1e3a8339","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_df51aae3f175421d903583b0","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants to debug why there's no serial output. They want to modify the code to make an LED blink at 1 second interval after flashing NuttX, so they can verify the firmware is actually running.\n\nLet me check the contest_board code and the LED definitions to understand which GPIO pins are used for LEDs.\n\nFrom the summary:\n- LD5: PG10 (Red)\n- LD6: PG0 (Green)  \n- LD7: PG8 (Blue)\n\nThe user wants a simple LED blink test in the main startup code. I should modify the `stm32_board_initialize()` function in `stm32_boot.c` to add a simple LED blink loop. This will run very early in the boot process, before any serial initialization, so it's a good way to verify the code is actually executing.\n\nLet me look at the current code and provide a simple LED blink implementation.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":1453,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":88256}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"bae03d78-2eb6-4701-875d-6784ac602b48","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:08:36.472Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
