{"parentUuid":"85297a5c-4a36-4a67-804a-f598324d7ef5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_8a3bb985409f44c6ab0eae90","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the LED definitions:- LD5: PG10 (Red)\n- LD6: PG0 (Green)\n- LD7: PG8 (Blue)When the I/O is LOW, the LED is on. When the I/O is HIGH, the LED is off.\n\nI need to modify `stm32_board_initialize()` to add a simple LED blink loop. This function runs very early in the boot process, so if the LED blinks, it means the code is executing.The STM32N6 runs at 200MHz according to board.h. I need to create a simple delay loop. Let me write a simple LED blink test.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":1039,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":90816}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"fe409cec-531e-4191-a085-88c51f346294","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:08:48.627Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"fe409cec-531e-4191-a085-88c51f346294","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_8a3bb985409f44c6ab0eae90","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"text","text":"现在修改 `stm32_boot.c`，在最早期的启动代码中加入 LED 闪烁测试："}],"usage":{"input_tokens":1039,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":90816}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"f8c8418d-22b9-4234-9b30-147624d6a8b6","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:08:49.038Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
{"parentUuid":"f8c8418d-22b9-4234-9b30-147624d6a8b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"id":"msg_8a3bb985409f44c6ab0eae90","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"mimo-v2.5-pro","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_119b55304aec485b952f91bd","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/warner/openvela/contest2026_224_quanyuanzhirendui/board/contest_board/src/stm32_boot.c","old_string":"#include <nuttx/config.h>\n\n#include <debug.h>\n\n#include <nuttx/board.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"contest_board.h\"\n\n#include <arch/board/board.h>\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32_board_initialize\n *\n * Description:\n *   All STM32 architectures must provide the following entry point.  This\n *   entry point is called early in the initialization -- after all memory\n *   has been configured and mapped but before any devices have been\n *   initialized.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32_board_initialize(void)\n{\n#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS\n  /* Configure on-board LEDs if LED support has been selected. */\n\n  board_autoled_initialize();\n#endif\n}","new_string":"#include <nuttx/config.h>\n\n#include <debug.h>\n\n#include <nuttx/board.h>\n\n#include \"arm_internal.h\"\n#include \"contest_board.h\"\n#include \"stm32_gpio.h\"\n\n#include <arch/board/board.h>\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Private Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/* Simple busy-wait delay. At 200MHz, each loop iteration is ~5 cycles.\n * 20000000 iterations ≈ 500ms at 200MHz.\n */\n\nstatic inline void delay_loop(volatile uint32_t count)\n{\n  while (count-- > 0)\n    {\n      __asm__ volatile(\"nop\");\n    }\n}\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Public Functions\n ****************************************************************************/\n\n/****************************************************************************\n * Name: stm32_board_initialize\n *\n * Description:\n *   All STM32 architectures must provide the following entry point.  This\n *   entry point is called early in the initialization -- after all memory\n *   has been configured and mapped but before any devices have been\n *   initialized.\n *\n ****************************************************************************/\n\nvoid stm32_board_initialize(void)\n{\n  /* LED blink test: verify code is running on the board.\n   *\n   * LD6 (PG0, Green) blinks at ~1Hz (500ms on, 500ms off).\n   * This runs in a loop forever to indicate the CPU is alive.\n   *\n   * LED active LOW: pin LOW = LED on, pin HIGH = LED off.\n   */\n\n  /* Configure LD6 (PG0) as output */\n\n  stm32_configgpio(GPIO_LD6);\n\n  /* Infinite blink loop - if you see the LED blinking, the CPU is running */\n\n  for (; ; )\n    {\n      /* LED ON (active low) */\n\n      stm32_gpiowrite(GPIO_LD6, false);\n      delay_loop(2000000);\n\n      /* LED OFF */\n\n      stm32_gpiowrite(GPIO_LD6, true);\n      delay_loop(2000000);\n    }\n\n#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_LEDS\n  /* Configure on-board LEDs if LED support has been selected. */\n\n  board_autoled_initialize();\n#endif\n}"}}],"usage":{"input_tokens":1039,"output_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":90816}},"type":"assistant","uuid":"7cae5b1e-2c08-4923-ab08-6c3884bc974c","timestamp":"2026-08-21T14:08:57.453Z","effort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-vscode","cwd":"/home/warner/openvela","sessionId":"6ad13cb3-6473-4031-a8c5-8ad621057323","version":"2.1.237","gitBranch":"HEAD","slug":"synthetic-wandering-llama"}
